WEBVTT

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:17.590
I know this cold voice

00:00:17.590 --> 00:00:22.020
Taking my friend

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:26.800
Maybe a little afraid you'll run away

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.700
But right now...

00:00:30.690 --> 00:00:34.720
For this moment in time, I want to hold you tight

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:39.580
By your side, I'm dreaming of the days

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:44.060
When I finally look up at the promised sky

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:48.470
I'll take off and break all the way

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.420
For this moment in time, I just wanna be with you

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:57.940
By your side, I'm dreaming of the days

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:02.250
When I finally look up at the promised sky

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:06.750
I know I can change all the way

00:01:07.270 --> 00:01:11.830
For the moment...

00:01:11.830 --> 00:01:21.320
I just wanna hold you...

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:32.850
Don't see that man again.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.060
Why not? Dad chose Eugene, didn't he?

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.210
What, choose that murderer?

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:39.930
Murderer?

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:43.270
He's already led three women to suicide.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:53.170
You've made an enemy, my Chinese friend.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.360
<b>"A Sleepless Night"</b>

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:03.170
Tyrant!

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.000
This is my house!

00:02:06.690 --> 00:02:08.780
Wrong. It's Harry's house.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:12.900
And while he's away on business, he's put me in charge.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:14.680
Lee-Leng!

00:02:15.590 --> 00:02:16.680
Lee-Leng!

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:18.680
--This is cruel!
--Toranosuke.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.040
--Hey!
--For the time being, don't let her out.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.040
--Hey, are you listening?
--Y--yes, sir.

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:25.820
--Lee-Leng!
--Zao. Keep investigating Volkan.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:29.340
--Argh! Lee-Leng!
--He's a deadly flower, but the deeper we dig, the more dirt we'll find.

00:02:29.510 --> 00:02:30.500
Got it.

00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:33.440
Even if he was mistakenly chosen,

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.890
I'll do everything in my power to get in his way!

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:42.450
What's gotten into Master Lee-Leng? I thought nothing could shake him up.

00:02:45.160 --> 00:02:46.700
Unbelievable.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.890
I had more freedom than this on Givoli!

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.290
Who would have thought Lee-Leng could hate anyone this much?

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.310
But... I think... I've seen this before...

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.660
Oh!

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.000
You... don't you work on the Burnsworth estate?

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:32.980
I have a little favor to ask...

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:44.000
Eugene... he's not going to take this lying down.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:51.660
How is Kajika?

00:03:52.490 --> 00:03:54.410
Staying quietly in her room.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.560
Master Lee-Leng.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:04:01.350
We've just heard from Malaysia. There's an issue with the buy-out.

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.910
It seems we've been put in a difficult position.

00:04:06.490 --> 00:04:07.980
Of all times...

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.820
I'll go there and conduct negotiations in person.

00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.950
I can't confirm this, but...

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:19.220
There is a faction within the Huang Group that, for trivial reasons,

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:22.740
intends to undermine your authority.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.350
I know.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:31.270
<i>Singapore</i>

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:39.430
"Burnsworth..."   Hmph.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:44.880
Just twenty years ago, it was only a tiny, insignificant oil company.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:49.890
That must cause your father some regret, eh?

00:04:51.380 --> 00:04:53.020
If you ask me, though...

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:59.830
I believe the Rosenthal name can again be the one heard around the world.

00:05:01.590 --> 00:05:04.570
So I want you to know, as his son,

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.790
in Singapore you will always have a friend in Tonsen Huang.

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.560
My thanks for your... kind offer.

00:05:18.390 --> 00:05:19.690
Dinner is served, Miss.

00:05:20.990 --> 00:05:23.050
I couldn't possibly eat.

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.320
Now, don't say that...

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:31.080
Being watched like this, on top of everything else...

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:33.080
Please make it fast.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:41.740
Let's eat something, shall we, and give Master Lee-Leng some relief?

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:50.860
Mustafa!

00:05:56.030 --> 00:05:57.590
Twelve o'clock...

00:05:59.990 --> 00:06:01.520
Very interesting.

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.190
Master Lee-Leng, your tea is ready.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:22.480
Kajika?

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.220
I think she's already in bed.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:41.380
Miss Kajika!

00:06:45.010 --> 00:06:46.020
Miss Kajika!

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:47.470
Sorry, Toranosuke!

00:06:49.170 --> 00:06:50.680
What happened? A blackout?

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.260
Master Lee-Leng!

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:56.960
We've been tricked! Miss Kajika got out of her room.

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:00.710
Where did she go? We have to split up and search!

00:07:01.870 --> 00:07:04.080
It's me. Don't let Kajika leave!

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.750
Miss Kajika?

00:07:08.390 --> 00:07:09.960
Understood.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:13.340
What's that?

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:16.900
Move, move!

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.120
Stop, Miss!

00:07:22.780 --> 00:07:24.790
Miss, please come down from there!

00:07:25.720 --> 00:07:27.420
Cain! Abel! Stop them!

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.470
Hey! Stop it!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:35.810
Get away! Shoo! Shoo!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:42.230
Eugene!

00:07:43.720 --> 00:07:45.170
Get in!

00:07:45.170 --> 00:07:46.680
Kajika!

00:07:46.860 --> 00:07:49.600
Sorry, Lee-Leng! Be back soon!

00:07:52.750 --> 00:07:54.260
Kajika!

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:58.830
Eugene! The damned, deadly flower!

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.570
Master Lee-Leng!

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:03.780
All of the cars have had their tires slashed!

00:08:04.490 --> 00:08:05.750
Call in the city police!

00:08:07.720 --> 00:08:09.870
We'll corner off all of New York.

00:08:11.130 --> 00:08:12.770
Use whatever you have!

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:15.570
Find them within the hour!

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.510
Y--Yes, sir...

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.930
Just wait.

00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:23.310
You wanted to see what I'd do if you really got me mad?

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.550
You're about to find out!

00:08:40.830 --> 00:08:42.960
Not--not good...

00:08:45.260 --> 00:08:47.270
This is bad, Miss Kajika.

00:08:47.560 --> 00:08:51.740
Seeing someone so mild-mannered get so angry... it's terrifying!

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:13.380
This is like a ghost's house.

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:16.350
You like all the space..

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:20.710
Being here, pitch black, covered in dust... it calms me.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:23.210
It's like melting into the dark.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:27.030
Leopards are nocturnal.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:29.540
Oh, no.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:32.620
Are you still fixated on that crazy idea?

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.600
Fixated... for good.

00:09:40.330 --> 00:09:41.810
And because of that idea,

00:09:42.340 --> 00:09:44.610
you'd come away with me in the dead of night.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:49.500
Eugene... did you take me away just to annoy Lee-Leng?

00:09:51.210 --> 00:09:52.670
Hm. I wonder...

00:09:54.780 --> 00:09:58.170
But then, I can imagine Mr. Burnsworth's anger.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:01.110
His guardian humiliated..

00:10:01.990 --> 00:10:06.220
his beloved daughter kidnapped by a man with a reputation like mine, a bad man.

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:09.130
Your reputation...

00:10:09.950 --> 00:10:12.390
You mean how they say you drove three women to suicide?

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:15.420
They all make their own choice to die.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:18.820
I wonder why people get so territorial...

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:22.220
I love you, so be with me.

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:25.260
I love you, so don't see anyone else.

00:10:26.520 --> 00:10:28.660
I love you, so love me back.

00:10:29.500 --> 00:10:31.100
It's like some kind of spell.

00:10:33.390 --> 00:10:36.110
For me, it's almost too awful to bear.

00:10:37.150 --> 00:10:40.910
These women think the word "love" absolves all sins.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:44.620
And then sometimes I find myself saying,

00:10:45.710 --> 00:10:47.110
"Why not just die?"

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:58.450
You don't tell them to die...

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.990
You say it just like you did to that woman.

00:11:02.790 --> 00:11:04.100
Kill one or the other.

00:11:05.720 --> 00:11:09.450
And then... they all choose themselves.

00:11:12.360 --> 00:11:13.800
It's almost like you're waiting...

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.430
for one of them to choose you.

00:11:19.780 --> 00:11:20.620
Why?

00:11:21.540 --> 00:11:23.510
Being alive is a wonderful thing!

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:27.850
Every life is a miracle against unbelievable odds!

00:11:28.390 --> 00:11:29.810
Why don't you treasure it?

00:11:32.030 --> 00:11:33.880
You call it wonderful.

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:37.350
You make it sound so simple.

00:11:38.590 --> 00:11:40.380
Where does that confidence come from?

00:11:42.050 --> 00:11:45.240
Certainly, there's nothing a Burnsworth can't do.

00:11:45.890 --> 00:11:47.260
Everything can be bought.

00:11:48.380 --> 00:11:49.700
Love, respect...

00:11:50.630 --> 00:11:52.410
even a person's reason for living.

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:57.380
If you wanted me to be Mustafa, you could buy me.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:01.090
Just ask Daddy, and it's all settled.

00:12:04.810 --> 00:12:06.760
I don't understand, Eugene.

00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:10.050
I just like you.

00:12:10.820 --> 00:12:12.780
What does buying have to do with anything?

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:15.320
Is that really what you think?

00:12:25.960 --> 00:12:27.010
Eugene.

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.180
I was raised on Givoli Island.

00:12:32.180 --> 00:12:36.760
When the seas are rough there, the island is completely isolated.

00:12:37.950 --> 00:12:40.850
No planes reach it. No boats will approach it.

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:46.760
At times like that, Maria would tell me that the island was in God's hands.

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:51.540
Nothing around you but the jet-black sky, no sound but the wind.

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:55.770
In a place like that, money had no meaning.

00:12:56.770 --> 00:12:59.600
The same wind blows on everyone.

00:13:00.860 --> 00:13:04.590
Caught between sky, land, and sea...

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.440
we could do nothing but wait for our fates.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:13.810
I would always wait with Mustafa for the storm to pass...

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.480
wondering, "What if?"

00:13:18.420 --> 00:13:19.390
What if?

00:13:20.190 --> 00:13:22.810
What if the wind never stopped...

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:24.780
if the waves never died down...

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:27.780
if we even ran out of food.

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:30.800
Many things ran through my head.

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.810
Half joking, but only half.

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:40.410
Could I lay down my life for Mustafa?

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:43.900
What a strange voice...

00:13:44.260 --> 00:13:48.500
I would never see Lee-Leng, or Dad, or Maria again...

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:52.250
It would be very sad... but he mattered so much...

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:56.900
a young boy's voice... a girl's...

00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:59.820
clear, but warm.

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:05.940
I would do it if it meant Mustafa could live.  That's what I always decided in the end.

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:10.970
Here he is!

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.780
Meet my brothers.

00:14:15.420 --> 00:14:19.200
Obviously it was a mistake to let you out of my sight.

00:14:20.340 --> 00:14:22.510
You made another fine mess for us to clean up.

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.650
You mean Reese?

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:28.880
I know nothing I say will do any good.

00:14:29.540 --> 00:14:31.470
Go back to the apartment, and get ready!

00:14:32.340 --> 00:14:36.200
Even without this little visit, I was planning on leaving tomorrow.

00:14:37.570 --> 00:14:39.390
The day after tomorrow is my birthday, after all.

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:44.160
I guess even a guy like you remembers his own birthday.

00:14:45.110 --> 00:14:47.210
Sure, especially this year.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:50.510
I ought to remember my twentieth birthday.

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.510
As of then, you'll be an adult.

00:14:53.930 --> 00:14:56.550
I can only pray you shape up!

00:14:57.620 --> 00:14:58.970
Don't talk to him like that!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:01.920
What is this kid doing here?

00:15:02.120 --> 00:15:03.370
I'm not a kid!

00:15:03.780 --> 00:15:06.560
She's Kajika Burnsworth.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:08.590
Burnsworth?!

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:15.910
Bastard! On top of everything, you would seduce Burnsworth's daughter?

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:18.150
Are you trying to destroy the Volkan Group?

00:15:22.050 --> 00:15:23.800
I can't stand to look at you!

00:15:24.440 --> 00:15:27.830
When our father dies, you'll lose his protection!

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:32.810
You'd better realize, your position as the next Chairman? It's a house built on sand!

00:15:35.560 --> 00:15:39.570
What makes you think I'm going to outlive our father?

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:45.890
What's that sound?

00:15:47.550 --> 00:15:48.660
P--president!

00:15:49.160 --> 00:15:50.730
What's all this commotion?

00:15:51.010 --> 00:15:53.340
The police have surrounded the house.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:54.790
What?!

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:10.430
It must be Lee-Leng! I'll handle him!

00:16:12.680 --> 00:16:13.640
Lee-Leng!

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:16.190
Handle me?

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:18.390
Not possible.

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.050
I see you're from the Volkan family.

00:16:23.110 --> 00:16:27.160
I'm sorry to say we will have to press charges against your younger brother.

00:16:27.700 --> 00:16:29.140
Charges?

00:16:29.760 --> 00:16:30.770
Lee-Leng!

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:36.340
Couldn't we find another way? Even if he's still a Volkan...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:40.700
Is that how you've covered up the other incidents?

00:16:42.420 --> 00:16:45.370
Stop it! Eugene hasn't done anything wrong.

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:49.400
I came here today on my own.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:51.960
Kajika...

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:58.910
Eugene...

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:02.690
Excuse me. It's just so funny...

00:17:03.900 --> 00:17:05.920
With the prosecution and the defense here...

00:17:06.680 --> 00:17:08.640
it's like I'm already standing trial.

00:17:09.910 --> 00:17:11.420
If you're going to press charges, do it quickly.

00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:14.970
In less than four hours I'm leaving for Paris.

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:20.400
Goodbye, Kajika.

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:22.290
It's been fun.

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.600
Eugene...

00:17:24.910 --> 00:17:27.920
Givoli during a storm... I wish I could've been there, too.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:30.560
But...

00:17:30.870 --> 00:17:33.320
Your Mustafa... I'm not him.

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:36.600
Don't be fooled by appearances.

00:17:37.690 --> 00:17:40.770
A stuffed animal with shiny silver fur is still full of sawdust.

00:17:41.960 --> 00:17:44.210
I'm no different.

00:17:46.060 --> 00:17:47.530
Eugene!

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.070
Kajika.

00:17:55.140 --> 00:17:57.000
I hate the new you!

00:17:57.300 --> 00:18:00.160
I might as well be with my guards on the island!

00:18:03.450 --> 00:18:04.740
Miss Kajika!

00:18:28.810 --> 00:18:29.680
Feeling better?

00:18:31.240 --> 00:18:33.210
Feeling sad... for Eugene.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:35.860
It's almost like...

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:39.190
the end of his life is the only thing he can see.

00:18:40.520 --> 00:18:43.650
Maybe that's what makes him so painfully beautiful.

00:18:44.540 --> 00:18:47.200
And if that's the case, who needs that kind of beauty?

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:49.680
Do you like Eugene?

00:18:50.660 --> 00:18:52.120
Yes.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:54.580
But I don't know what kind of "like" it is.

00:19:00.100 --> 00:19:00.890
Lee-Leng,

00:19:02.380 --> 00:19:03.980
Stop the investigation.

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:09.340
I'm not interested in Eugene's past.

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:12.660
There's no point in digging that stuff up.

00:19:13.580 --> 00:19:14.630
The present is plenty.

00:19:15.890 --> 00:19:18.640
But I have to confront him...

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:20.640
and there isn't a moment to lose.

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.960
Well, then, go to Paris.

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:27.520
As soon as my business is done, I'll come, too.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:32.790
You have to get to the bottom of this "like" of yours.

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:35.670
Lee-Leng!

00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:42.030
I'm sorry.

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:44.030
I said terrible things to you before.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:47.300
It's alright.

00:19:49.470 --> 00:19:52.310
I want to get to Paris as quickly as I can.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.310
What Eugene said earlier...

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:02.350
that he might die before his father does...

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.100
For some reason, it really worries me.

00:20:16.740 --> 00:20:18.660
The position as Chairman... are you going to accept?

00:20:19.770 --> 00:20:22.330
I belong to my father; all I can do is obey his orders.

00:20:23.810 --> 00:20:27.210
Besides, I'm well aware that I'm purely ornamental.

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:30.110
The one with the grip on family affairs is you, brother.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:34.530
I think the stockholders' meeting will wrap up smoothly.

00:20:36.760 --> 00:20:37.970
I don't get it.

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.400
A guy like you, I just can't understand.

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:53.500
The rising sun...

00:20:54.310 --> 00:20:56.480
it's usually linked to the empty noise of the morning.

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.460
But, if this one is to be my last...

00:21:01.730 --> 00:21:04.530
I think I'll watch this one with deeper feelings for once.

00:21:08.080 --> 00:21:12.100
<b>Malaysia</b>

00:21:12.860 --> 00:21:15.310
I understand Miss Kajika said it wouldn't be necessary...

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:18.480
but the investigation of Eugene has produced something strange.

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:21.900
Here, please look this over.

00:21:31.330 --> 00:21:32.390
We're losing the light.

00:21:33.120 --> 00:21:35.140
This is all because you said to take that dirt road.

00:21:35.950 --> 00:21:38.510
No, but it's definitely somewhere around here.

00:21:39.290 --> 00:21:41.370
You make one odd bodyguard.

00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:43.650
Not to mention your baby face.

00:21:44.530 --> 00:21:46.500
What does my baby face have to do with this?

00:21:49.350 --> 00:21:51.420
--Excuse me!
--Miss Kajika!

00:21:54.910 --> 00:21:57.390
Excuse me, I'm trying to get to the Volkan estate.

00:22:00.570 --> 00:22:02.260
Please forgive me, but who might you be?

00:22:03.160 --> 00:22:06.730
I am the butler for the Volkan house. You may call me Orbach.

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:09.400
The butler?

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:12.150
I'm Kajika Burnsworth.

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:14.240
I've come to see Eugene.

00:22:15.730 --> 00:22:17.470
Master Eugene?

00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:20.930
One way or another, there's something I need to find out for certain.

00:22:22.860 --> 00:22:25.010
Eugene's mother, Kristin...

00:22:25.610 --> 00:22:27.430
Mr. Volkan's third wife.

00:22:28.480 --> 00:22:32.750
She was the one who carried Eugene, but she died not long after he was born.

00:22:33.990 --> 00:22:37.350
Now, this information comes from private Huang sources...

00:22:37.850 --> 00:22:41.980
but it seems Mr. Volkan, five years before Eugene's birth, had an accident...

00:22:41.980 --> 00:22:44.820
which rendered him unable to have more children.

00:22:50.130 --> 00:22:54.460
In other words... Eugene is not Mr. Volkan's son!

00:23:01.780 --> 00:23:08.380
I can't stand feeling this distance,

00:23:09.150 --> 00:23:16.210
So I'm starting to search for your heart.

00:23:16.700 --> 00:23:22.790
Because you were always at my side, protecting me.

00:23:23.450 --> 00:23:28.020
And I'm afraid of being alone.

00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:37.280
Though it's been a long time, everyone's just the same.

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:44.720
Whether sleeping now, or crying, I want to see your smiling face.

00:23:44.720 --> 00:23:52.240
Because I will love you, with heart overflowing.

00:23:52.240 --> 00:23:59.330
Don't turn away, look at me. I believe in you.

00:23:59.910 --> 00:24:06.860
So, no one else knows our secret thoughts

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:14.240
The blue sea of a strong and beautiful time.

00:24:14.590 --> 00:24:24.380
In those arms, in that embrace, I'm alive.
